index 6879bd825ea3d005af6228c9fdde0193c65af0dd..c4d25681eb26de58d587c838d26968e55cb46c80 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -12,6 +12,21 @@ Build and interface details: [documentation](https://unixnu.com/drivers/adreno-m
 
 Unused owned image backing can serve later pooled or dedicated images. Extra image spares share a 256 MiB device budget and expire after ten seconds. Plain unused backing of at least 256 KiB can be released by the existing room worker, with at most 128 MiB queued. Allocation failure reclaims queued backing before retrying. Imported memory and owner callbacks retain their release ordering.
 
+## GPU scanout conversion
+
+`shaders/scanout_convert.ll` retains separate half-float (`scanout_convert`) and opaque BGRA (`scanout_opaque`) kernels and adds `scanout_b3a8` for `NGP_B3A8_XR_OPAQUE` (format 4). Its buffers are source 0, destination 1 and 16-byte parameters 3: width, height, source pitch in words, destination pitch in words. For format 4 only, `Frame.stride` is the alpha plane's **byte** stride, which is also the colour plane's pitch in 32-bit words; do not divide it by four. Plane 0 holds XRGB2101010 with R at bit 20, G at bit 10 and B at bit 0. The kernel clips each code to `[384,894]`, rounds XR to eight bits, and stores opaque BGRX without gamma, a lookup table or alpha-plane reads. Import validation still requires the complete two-plane extent, including alpha at `align_up(4 * stride * height, 4096)`.
+
+The Linux regression executes the actual new IR function after adapting its target and address spaces, verifies the complete AIR with `llvm-as` and `opt`, and runs O0, O2 and ASan/UBSan checks. It covers all 1024 codes per channel, boundary colour combinations, partial workgroups, inaccessible alpha pages, poisoned padding, output canaries and the 1080×2340 / stride-1088 layout. Run from this repository:
+
+```sh
+python3 bridge/check_scanout_b3a8.py
+python3 bridge/check_scanout_b3a8.py --reference-header /path/to/NativeLegacyRequest.h
+```
+
+The optional header is the consuming display driver's existing CPU reference and is included only at test compile time; the test does not copy it into this repository. Without it the test uses an independent rational XR oracle and says so. ASan instruments the adapted IR's memory accesses; UBSan applies to the C harness and optional C reference, not retroactively to LLVM arithmetic. These are CPU executions of shader IR, not GPU qualification.
+
+The existing resolved-tree `python3 scripts/check-native-metal-frontend-host.py` builds and runs `bridge/scanout_host.mm` through the real frontend, translator and host Vulkan device. Its b3a8 cases retain the half-float and BGRA checks, vary alpha independently, check every output pixel and padding, and present twice to reuse each compiled pipeline. Cold/warm persistent shader-cache runs remain separate invocations of that host check. `bridge/present_host.mm` expects opaque alpha on the native compute path but preserves original alpha for the `NMB_SYSTEM_DEVICE=1` blit baseline. A missing host GPU is not a pixel-test pass, and neither host test establishes Adreno hardware completion or scanout correctness.
+
 ## Frame diagnostics
 
 With `sheng-gpu-trace=1` the render server writes its frame trace (command phases, encoding batches, memory decisions, completion stages, attachments and Turnip pass and submission records) to its own file. Only event 63, the render, encode and completion thread identities, reaches the kernel ring. See [GPU frame diagnostics](https://unixnu.com/porting/gpu-diagnostics) for fields and decoding.
